 "comment": [
  "Module classification for scripts/check-layering.py (goal jaune-shape-and-names-v1, S0, unit W0).",
  "specification: defines the EVM; no #guard, no example, no test helper, no fixture vocabulary except the listed residue.",
  "proof: theorems about the specification (derivations, projections, arithmetic); built on specification and proof modules.",
  "check: #guard / example / test helpers and consumer examples; compiled by the default build.",
  "adapter: runner, fixture and tracer front ends; they may import anything.",
  "implementation: a second implementation kept for speed; a specification module imports one only where listed in implementation_imports.",
  "bridge: old and new definitions side by side at a convergence gate (3.1), with the bridge theorems and the maps and invariants they use; deleted after the gate's tagged commit.",
  "fixture_vocabulary_residue: rejection tags and renderers that still sit in specification modules. evm_halt_kinds stay by decision (the tracer prints them; a failed checked system call puts them in the block's rejection text). called_by_specification are reached by specification functions that return rendered text (stateTransitionAt, stateTransitionUsing, rlpToBlock, ImportOutcome.renderLegacy); since the G0b structured-cause cut, processCheckedSystemTransaction and validateOmmerWithParent return systemContractCallFailed and invalidOmmerHeader and call no renderer, and BlockValidationError.detail writes their text. The list leaves with the chain-transition variants (S6c) and only shrinks."
 ],
